{"name":"California Girl","hex":"#fca716","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"girl","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A female child.","A woman, especially a young and often attractive woman."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To feminize or girlify; to gender as a girl or as for girls.","To staff with or as a girl or girls."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/girl"}],"entries":[{"title":"California Gurls","blocks":[{"text":"\"California Gurls\" is a song by American singer Katy Perry from her third studio album, Teenage Dream (2010). It was released as the album's lead single on May 7, 2010, through Capitol Records. The song features rap verses from Snoop Dogg. They both co-wrote \"California Gurls\" with Bonnie McKee and its producers Dr. Luke, Max Martin, and Benny Blanco. The track was recorded at Conway Recording Studios, based in Hollywood, Los Angeles. The song's mid-tempo production contains disco-pop and electropop. Its lyrics are an ode to the state of California, in which both Perry and Snoop Dogg were born and raised. According to Perry, \"California Gurls\" is an answer song to \"Empire State of Mind\" by Jay-Z and Alicia Keys."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/84/California_Gurls_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California_Gurls"},{"title":"California","blocks":[{"text":"California is a state in the Western United States. It is bordered by Oregon to the north, the Mexican state of Baja California to the south, Nevada to the east, Arizona to the southeast, and the Pacific Ocean to the west. With a population of over 39 million across an area of 163,696 square miles (423,970 km2), it is the most populous U.S. state and the third largest by land area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Flag_of_California.svg/330px-Flag_of_California.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California"},{"title":"Girl","blocks":[{"text":"A girl is a young female human, usually a child or an adolescent. While the term girl has other meanings, including young woman, daughter, or girlfriend regardless of age, the first meaning is the most common one."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Young_girl_smiling_in_sunshine_%282%29.jpg/330px-Young_girl_smiling_in_sunshine_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Girl"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/84/California_Gurls_cover.png/250px-California_Gurls_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/84/California_Gurls_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/84/California_Gurls_cover.png/250px-California_Gurls_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACalifornia_Gurls_cover.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Snoop_Dogg_on_Stage.jpg/500px-Snoop_Dogg_on_Stage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Snoop_Dogg_on_Stage.jpg/1280px-Snoop_Dogg_on_Stage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Snoop_Dogg_on_Stage.jpg/500px-Snoop_Dogg_on_Stage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Perry found Snoop Dogg as a rapper with whom to collaborate on \"California Gurls\" through a search on Wikipedia.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASnoo